<programme start="20261107050000 +0000" stop="20261107080000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">South Florida at East Carolina</sub-title><desc lang="en">The South Florida Bulls (6-2) visit the East Carolina Pirates (4-4) at Dowdy-Ficklen Stadium for an American Conference matchup. South Florida seeks its third straight win after beating UAB 30-10, while East Carolina enters after beating Temple 17-9.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261107080000 +0000" stop="20261107110000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">TCU at Arizona</sub-title><desc lang="en">The TCU Horned Frogs (4-4) face the No. 24 Arizona Wildcats (6-2) at Casino Del Sol Stadium in a Big 12 matchup. TCU enters after defeating Kansas 22-16 behind Jaden Craig, while Arizona fell 34-26 to Texas Tech and relies on quarterback Noah Fifita.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261107110000 +0000" stop="20261107140000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Virginia Tech at SMU</sub-title><desc lang="en">The SMU Mustangs (6-2) host the Virginia Tech Hokies (6-2) at Gerald J. Ford Stadium in an ACC matchup. Virginia Tech seeks its third straight win after beating Clemson 20-16, while SMU fell to Syracuse 30-27 and relies on quarterback Kevin Jennings.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261107140000 +0000" stop="20261107170000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College GameDay</title><desc lang="en">Originating from the site of Saturday&apos;s biggest games, host Rece Davis and analysts Kirk Herbstreit, Desmond Howard, Pat McAfee, and Nick Saban cover college football with pregame breakdowns, exclusive interviews, features and predictions.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p629309_b_s4_ac.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261107170000 +0000" stop="20261107200000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Tulsa at Tulane</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Green Wave (4-4, 2-2 American) go for their fourth straight victory over the Golden Hurricane (4-4, 1-3). Tulane has claimed six of the last eight meetings after a 31-14 verdict in 2025. The Green Wave have alternated losses and wins all season.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261107200000 +0000" stop="20261107203000 +0000" channel="ESPN U"><title lang="en">TrueSouth</title><sub-title lang="en">Shreveport</sub-title><desc lang="en">Herby K&apos;s is a 1936 vintage beer garden and fry house; Lucky Palace serves wok-fried t-bones and pork egg foo young; both of these restaurants are survivors, like Shreveport itself.</desc><category lang="en">Travel</category><category lang="en">Food</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p15917551_b_v11_ab.jpg"/></programme>
