<programme start="20261107160000 +0000" stop="20261107170000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">Big Noon Kickoff</title><desc lang="en">College football pregame show covering the top college football games from the country&apos;s best conferences, beginning each Saturday on FOX.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p17245398_b_v12_ap.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261107170000 +0000" stop="20261107203000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Iowa State at Baylor</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Bears (5-3, 3-2 Big 12) brace for Aiden Flora and the Cyclones (4-4, 2-3). Baylor leads the series 12-11 after Iowa State prevailed 43-21 in 2024. Flora rushed for 221 yards and two touchdowns in a 51-49 triumph over Oklahoma State last week.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261107203000 +0000" stop="20261108000000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Penn State at Washington</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Huskies (5-3, 2-3 Big Ten) try to solve the Nittany Lions (4-4, 1-4). Penn State has won all four meetings, the last a 35-6 decision in 2024. Both sides own double-digit victories over Purdue and one-score losses to No. 20 USC this season.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261108000000 +0000" stop="20261108020000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Providence vs. Nebraska</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Friars (1-0) and Cornhuskers (1-0) face off in a Basketball Hall of Fame Tip-Off game. The programs meet for the first time. Providence was picked to finish fifth in the Big East preseason poll. Nebraska was voted in the same spot in the Big Ten.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191260_b_v8_az.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261108020000 +0000" stop="20261108023000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">FS1 College Football Extra</title><desc lang="en">Highlights of the day&apos;s college football action.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p11000904_b_s3_ab.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261108023000 +0000" stop="20261108060000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Hawaii at Texas-El Paso</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Rainbow Warriors (2-6, 1-4) visit the Miners (1-7, 0-4) for a Mountain West affair. The programs haven&apos;t met since 2004, when they were Western Athletic Conference foes. Hawaii traveled 4,255 miles to beat Northern Illinois 56-21 last week.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261108060000 +0000" stop="20261108090000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">UCLA at Minnesota</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 8 UCLA Bruins (8-0) face the Minnesota Golden Gophers (5-3) at Huntington Bank Stadium for a Big Ten game. UCLA enters undefeated in eight games after shutting out Nevada 27-0, while Minnesota is coming off a 23-16 overtime defeat to Indiana.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261108090000 +0000" stop="20261108120000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Iowa at Northwestern</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 19 Hawkeyes seek their fifth straight victory over the Wildcats. Both sides are 6-2, 3-2 Big Ten. Iowa recorded its third shutout of the season, holding Wisconsin to nine first downs and 235 yards from scrimmage in a 30-0 decision last week.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261106110000 +0000" stop="20261106130000 +0000" channel="FS2 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Pennsylvania at Illinois</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Illinois Fighting Illini host the Pennsylvania Quakers at State Farm Center in Champaign. Illinois leads the all-time head-to-head series 7-0 against Pennsylvania, highlighted by a 105-70 win on March 19, 2026, in the NCAA Tournament first round.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191260_b_v8_az.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261106130000 +0000" stop="20261106150000 +0000" channel="FS2 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">Women&apos;s College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">UConn at Michigan</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Michigan Wolverines and the UConn Huskies face off in a regular-season game at Crisler Center. UConn leads the all-time head-to-head series 1-0 against Michigan, winning the Nov. 21, 2025, game 72-69. Fope Ayo leads the Wolverines in this game.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191292_b_v12_bh.jpg"/></programme>
